    "lawSection": "Oswego County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S246\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act in relation to authorizing the town of Schroeppel to repay to\ntaxpayers monies erroneously received by such town as a result of\noverpaid special assessments\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nAuthorizes the town of Schroeppel in Oswego County to repay to\ntaxpayers monies erroneously received by such town as a result of\noverpaid special assessments.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nAuthorizes repayment of monies to certain taxpayers of funds\nerroneously received by the town of Schroeppel as a result of taxes\ncollected pursuant to the 2005 assessment roll based on inaccurate\ninformation.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe 2005 town budget was adopted and submitted to the Oswego County\nTreasurer containing transcriptional errors on the summary page for\nthree water districts and one sewer district in the town of\nSchroeppel.  The error involved applying amounts that should have been\ngeneral obligations of the town to the respective districts, thus\nincreasing the unit charge that appeared on the respective tax bills.\n\nThe town collected a significant amount of money which they are\nwilling to return back to the taxpayer. However, in order for them to\ndo this, special state legislation authorizing this action must be\nenacted.  Therefore, this measure would allow the town to refund the\novercharge in taxes back to the citizens of those impacted districts.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nS.7518 - 2005, Passed Senate.\nS.7105 - 2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
